WEBVTT

1
00:02:16.262 --> 00:02:17.472
It's getting late, Officer.

2
00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:57.473
Sheriff, you gotta
get down here.

3
00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:30.042
We got an ID on her?

4
00:03:30.336 --> 00:03:31.456
No, Sir.

5
00:03:31.754 --> 00:03:32.954
No relation to Paul and Carol.

6
00:03:38.177 --> 00:03:39.177
Who's she?

7
00:03:40.638 --> 00:03:42.258
Well, for now,
she's a Jane Doe.

8
00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.104
You got something?

9
00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:47.523
Nothing was stolen.

10
00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.731
Not a scratch on the outside
of the house either.

11
00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:52.821
Doesn't look like
someone broke in.

12
00:03:53.108 --> 00:03:55.648
To me, it looks like
they were trying to break out.

13
00:05:16.191 --> 00:05:20.321
" I hit the floor around 4:47
with the mornin' blues"

14
00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:22.492
" Cryin' like a puppy dog"

15
00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:24.241
" It takes some time
to come out"

16
00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.493
" Face the music
gotta pay your dues"

17
00:05:26.785 --> 00:05:30.365
" You're the only one I want"

18
00:05:30.664 --> 00:05:33.254
" Best time tonight
then I'm gonna cry"

19
00:05:33.542 --> 00:05:35.592
" Gotta put this right"

20
00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:37.708
" I've been dyin'"

21
00:05:38.005 --> 00:05:41.215
" Girl I just
ain't been feelin' right"

22
00:05:41.508 --> 00:05:43.888
" Yes I'm in trouble
I know it"

23
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:48.138
" You shot me down
burnin' like a heart attack"

24
00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:50.352
" All over you yeah"

25
00:05:50.642 --> 00:05:52.142
" My brown-eyed girl"

26
00:05:52.436 --> 00:05:53.846
" I guess I swear
her hair was"

27
00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:57.436
" I guess I swear her hair
was midnight black"

28
00:05:57.733 --> 00:06:00.613
" Midnight black
Oh yeah"

29
00:06:00.903 --> 00:06:02.783
" Midnight black
Oh yeah ""

30
00:06:03.072 --> 00:06:04.702
Cause of death?

31
00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.620
How about we
skip this part tonight?

32
00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.660
Come on,
this one's a soft ball.

33
00:06:13.248 --> 00:06:15.418
Smoke inhalation.

34
00:06:15.709 --> 00:06:19.209
You're telling me
that smoke killed Mr. Howard?

35
00:06:19.505 --> 00:06:21.755
Well, damaged nasal passage

36
00:06:22.049 --> 00:06:23.879
damaged throat, damaged lungs..

37
00:06:24.176 --> 00:06:25.426
Damaged lungs, yes.

38
00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:28.059
But incompatible with life.

39
00:06:28.347 --> 00:06:29.783
So, you're saying
that's not the COD?

40
00:06:29.807 --> 00:06:32.097
I'm saying
look before you leap.

41
00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:36.688
Where did the Police
find the body?

42
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.820
Uh, in his kitchen.

43
00:06:39.108 --> 00:06:41.818
House on fire.
Front door is 30 feet away

44
00:06:42.111 --> 00:06:43.431
Yet, he's not
trying to get there.

45
00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:45.237
Lungs are damaged

46
00:06:45.531 --> 00:06:47.831
but airways not denuded
nearly enough.

47
00:06:50.285 --> 00:06:51.365
So, he stopped breathing

48
00:06:51.662 --> 00:06:52.982
before that fire
really got going?

49
00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:56.714
Open him up.

50
00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:01.844
Now.

51
00:07:02.131 --> 00:07:03.131
Now you see here?

52
00:07:03.173 --> 00:07:05.763
Down below the occipital.
A fracture.

53
00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:09.613
That explains the swelling
in his brain.

54
00:07:09.847 --> 00:07:12.217
Subdural hematoma.

55
00:07:12.516 --> 00:07:15.226
That's what did it.
Not the smoke.

56
00:07:16.812 --> 00:07:18.982
Everybody has a secret.

57
00:07:19.273 --> 00:07:21.613
Some just hide them
better than others.

58
00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.570
Some people are better
at finding them.

59
00:07:24.862 --> 00:07:26.822
You did good.
You'll get there.

60
00:07:30.826 --> 00:07:33.696
Nobody's even
claimed him yet.

61
00:07:33.996 --> 00:07:35.348
He was all alone,
that's why he died.

62
00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:37.542
He died because
he fell and hit his head.

63
00:07:42.463 --> 00:07:44.593
You got plans tonight?

64
00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:46.882
Emma wants to go
see a movie at The Strand.

65
00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:50.758
I thought they'd closed
that place down.

66
00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:52.684
Uh, no, when was
the last time

67
00:07:52.973 --> 00:07:54.413
you even went to go
see a movie, Dad?

68
00:07:56.894 --> 00:07:59.524
Uh, she has Alzheimer's

69
00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:02.943
and he's building her a house.

70
00:08:04.193 --> 00:08:05.243
The Notebook?

71
00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:07.907
Oh, yeah, your mother made me
go and see it with her

72
00:08:08.197 --> 00:08:09.697
for her birthday.

73
00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.190
I fell asleep five minutes in.

74
00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:16.620
Yeah.

75
00:08:16.914 --> 00:08:18.084
Are you alright finishing up?

76
00:08:18.373 --> 00:08:19.503
Yeah.

77
00:08:23.212 --> 00:08:25.382
What's up, Tilden?

78
00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:27.302
Hematoma.

79
00:09:48.922 --> 00:09:49.972
Stanley.

80
00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:53.467
Oh.

81
00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.350
Hey, Dad!

82
00:09:59.641 --> 00:10:00.931
Stanley got another one.

83
00:10:11.028 --> 00:10:12.108
Dad?

84
00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.910
Jesus Christ!

85
00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.740
It's so easy!

86
00:11:00.035 --> 00:11:01.035
How'd you get down here?

87
00:11:01.203 --> 00:11:02.323
The key was in the elevator.

88
00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:04.749
Oh, my God.

89
00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.960
I gotta say, this is not
what I was expecting.

90
00:11:08.251 --> 00:11:10.841
You said it was old
but wow.

91
00:11:11.129 --> 00:11:13.089
I thought we were supposed
to meet out front.

92
00:11:13.382 --> 00:11:15.132
Well, I got tired of waiting.

93
00:11:15.425 --> 00:11:17.045
Where, where are you going?

94
00:11:17.344 --> 00:11:19.014
I'm having a little look.

95
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:20.764
Come back.

96
00:11:21.056 --> 00:11:22.926
God, the place
just keeps going.

97
00:11:23.225 --> 00:11:25.725
Well, three generations
of Tildens keep expanding

98
00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:28.309
end up with this
state-of-the-art facility.

99
00:11:28.605 --> 00:11:30.515
Hey, come on.

100
00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:32.226
What's the rush?

101
00:11:32.526 --> 00:11:34.026
I've been down here all day.

102
00:11:37.322 --> 00:11:40.372
You got to see me at my job,
why can't I see you at yours?

103
00:11:40.659 --> 00:11:41.949
You work at a book store.

104
00:11:56.007 --> 00:11:57.377
Are these all people?

105
00:11:57.676 --> 00:11:58.756
Just three tonight.

106
00:12:01.054 --> 00:12:02.054
Can I see one?

107
00:12:02.222 --> 00:12:04.772
Well, no. No.
You cannot see one.

108
00:12:05.058 --> 00:12:05.768
Why not?

109
00:12:06.059 --> 00:12:08.059
Because there's...

110
00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:10.363
Some things you can't
un-see, okay?

111
00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:11.897
Come on, I can handle it.

112
00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:15.360
No. No. And my dad
is way too strict.

113
00:12:15.652 --> 00:12:16.652
Try me.

114
00:12:18.822 --> 00:12:20.822
So, what'll it be?

115
00:12:22.868 --> 00:12:24.948
Are you serious?

116
00:12:25.245 --> 00:12:26.575
Are you?

117
00:12:26.872 --> 00:12:28.042
Hell yeah.

118
00:12:28.331 --> 00:12:29.331
Pick one.

119
00:12:48.685 --> 00:12:50.055
Not that one.

120
00:12:50.353 --> 00:12:51.353
The one next to it.

121
00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.440
A body's a body.

122
00:12:53.732 --> 00:12:55.112
Yeah, well, I pick that one.

123
00:13:20.258 --> 00:13:21.258
What's that for?

124
00:13:21.343 --> 00:13:23.603
To make sure he's dead.

125
00:13:23.887 --> 00:13:25.323
There used to be a time
it was hard to tell

126
00:13:25.347 --> 00:13:26.927
a comatose person
from a dead one.

127
00:13:27.224 --> 00:13:30.234
So coroners tied bells
to everybody in the morgue.

128
00:13:30.519 --> 00:13:31.519
So if they heard a 'ting'

129
00:13:31.561 --> 00:13:32.851
they knew somebody down there

130
00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:34.856
wasn't quite ready to go.

131
00:13:35.148 --> 00:13:36.148
So, why do you have one?

132
00:13:36.358 --> 00:13:39.608
Well, I'm... I'm a bit
of a traditionalist.

133
00:13:44.241 --> 00:13:45.321
Why did you cover his face?

134
00:13:45.408 --> 00:13:48.078
There wasn't much
of a face left to cover.

135
00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:51.370
Point blank gun shot blast
tend to do that.

136
00:13:51.665 --> 00:13:52.665
Who shot him?

137
00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:55.463
Angle of entry suggests
he did it to himself.

138
00:13:55.752 --> 00:13:58.552
until we found Strychnine
in his system

139
00:13:58.839 --> 00:14:01.150
And judging by the progress it
made through his bloodstream

140
00:14:01.174 --> 00:14:04.804
he was already dead by the time
somebody blew his face off.

141
00:14:05.095 --> 00:14:06.885
Why would anyone do that?

142
00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:08.890
You sound like
your boyfriend.

143
00:14:10.225 --> 00:14:12.095
Leave the "why" to the cops
and the shrinks.

144
00:14:12.394 --> 00:14:15.114
We're just here
to find cause of death.

145
00:14:15.397 --> 00:14:17.357
No more, no less.

146
00:14:27.742 --> 00:14:29.292
You don't wanna see that.

147
00:14:30.954 --> 00:14:32.214
It's alright.

148
00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:55.230
Look who's easy now.

149
00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.123
You should have seen
the look on your face.

150
00:14:57.147 --> 00:14:58.624
I can't wait to see
the look on your face

151
00:14:58.648 --> 00:14:59.750
when you're not
getting laid tonight.

152
00:14:59.774 --> 00:15:01.484
Whoa, whoa. Hold on.
Hold on. Hold on.

153
00:15:01.776 --> 00:15:04.606
Not even if I ply you
with popcorn and sourpatch kids?

154
00:15:07.157 --> 00:15:08.577
You're lucky you're cute.

155
00:15:10.911 --> 00:15:12.121
How do you get used to that?

156
00:15:14.539 --> 00:15:16.169
You do and you don't.

157
00:15:19.544 --> 00:15:20.594
Sheriff?

158
00:15:23.256 --> 00:15:25.176
Where's your dad?
What happened?

159
00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:26.757
Bring her back here,
Sheldon.

160
00:15:32.557 --> 00:15:33.757
Dad, if you need me to stay...

161
00:15:33.808 --> 00:15:34.848
Oh, don't worry about it.

162
00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:36.443
You two go have your fun.

163
00:15:48.239 --> 00:15:50.489
Did you see the look
on Burke's face?

164
00:15:50.784 --> 00:15:54.204
I mean, he wouldn't be here this
late if it wasn't important.

165
00:15:54.496 --> 00:15:55.206
Here we go.

166
00:15:55.497 --> 00:15:57.537
Well, my dad...
There it is.

167
00:15:57.832 --> 00:15:58.832
I can't ditch him.

168
00:15:58.875 --> 00:16:00.375
So you're ditching me again.

169
00:16:00.669 --> 00:16:02.299
What's he gonna do
when you leave?

170
00:16:05.715 --> 00:16:06.715
You haven't told him yet?

171
00:16:06.841 --> 00:16:08.801
No. It's not that simple.

172
00:16:09.094 --> 00:16:10.354
Wow.

173
00:16:10.637 --> 00:16:11.677
Babe.

174
00:16:11.972 --> 00:16:13.472
I'm gonna tell him, okay?

175
00:16:13.765 --> 00:16:15.675
Hey, you think
I wanna be here?

176
00:16:15.976 --> 00:16:17.516
Down there?

177
00:16:17.811 --> 00:16:18.851
This isn't my life.

178
00:16:19.145 --> 00:16:21.975
I don't wanna be Austin Tilden,
the morgue worker.

179
00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.860
Just, he needs my help
right now.

180
00:16:27.779 --> 00:16:29.659
Come on, it's been two years.

181
00:16:29.948 --> 00:16:31.488
He can take care of himself.

182
00:16:34.786 --> 00:16:36.246
Come back in a few hours.

183
00:16:36.538 --> 00:16:40.168
We'll catch the midnight show,
grab a drink at Thornton's..

184
00:16:40.458 --> 00:16:41.838
Two drinks.

185
00:16:42.127 --> 00:16:45.207
11 o'clock, I'm all yours.
I promise.

186
00:16:46.548 --> 00:16:47.838
And don't, you know,
don't smile

187
00:16:48.133 --> 00:16:49.573
because a smile
means "yes" you know.

188
00:16:51.219 --> 00:16:52.219
I know it's in there.

189
00:16:52.429 --> 00:16:53.949
Now, you're gonna
blow your whole game.

190
00:16:58.893 --> 00:17:00.153
Maybe.

191
00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.398
You're hot!

192
00:17:20.248 --> 00:17:23.078
Found her in the basement
of the Douglas' place.

193
00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:26.296
No ID, no fingerprints
in the system.

194
00:17:26.588 --> 00:17:28.298
No one has a clue
who she is.

195
00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.470
I don't suppose you know
how she wound up there?

196
00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:32.968
Stanley.

197
00:17:35.472 --> 00:17:37.392
Damn thing gets meaner
by the day.

198
00:17:39.851 --> 00:17:43.061
Alvarez there was working
at Paul and Carol's place.

199
00:17:43.354 --> 00:17:46.024
My best bet?
He killed our Jane Doe.

200
00:17:46.316 --> 00:17:47.856
Needed a place
to dump the body.

201
00:17:48.151 --> 00:17:49.781
Didn't count the Douglas'
being home

202
00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:51.240
or Paul having a.38.

203
00:17:51.529 --> 00:17:52.757
First thing tomorrow,
I'll bring him in

204
00:17:52.781 --> 00:17:54.021
but for now,
she's the priority.

205
00:17:54.199 --> 00:17:55.519
Oh, still, it would
have been nice

206
00:17:55.617 --> 00:17:56.897
to take a look
at the crime scene

207
00:18:03.625 --> 00:18:04.705
I got four people dead

208
00:18:05.001 --> 00:18:07.301
and no god damn clue
how any of it connects.

209
00:18:07.587 --> 00:18:10.337
Nobody's pissin'
in your grits here, Shel.

210
00:18:10.632 --> 00:18:11.932
But we do have protocol.

211
00:18:13.593 --> 00:18:16.353
Press is gonna need answers
on this in the morning

212
00:18:16.638 --> 00:18:17.638
and I got nothing.

213
00:18:22.268 --> 00:18:23.938
Now they'll buy a 10-79.

214
00:18:24.229 --> 00:18:26.519
I can give them
a B and E gone haywire.

215
00:18:26.815 --> 00:18:29.395
But what I can't sell is her.

216
00:18:32.612 --> 00:18:34.532
Time frame?

217
00:18:34.823 --> 00:18:36.373
It's gotta be tonight.

218
00:18:36.658 --> 00:18:37.658
Okay.

219
00:18:40.829 --> 00:18:42.249
You didn't have to come back.

220
00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:44.540
I know.

221
00:19:04.561 --> 00:19:07.111
This is the autopsy
of an unidentified female

222
00:19:07.397 --> 00:19:09.477
henceforth known as "Jane Doe."

223
00:19:09.774 --> 00:19:11.484
Performing the autopsy
will be myself

224
00:19:11.776 --> 00:19:13.396
Tommy Tilden,
attending coroner.

225
00:19:13.695 --> 00:19:16.065
I will be assisted
by Austin Tilden

226
00:19:16.364 --> 00:19:18.784
certified medical technician.

227
00:19:19.075 --> 00:19:22.195
This autopsy will be
conducted in four stages

228
00:19:22.495 --> 00:19:24.955
beginning with
an external evaluation

229
00:19:25.248 --> 00:19:26.788
followed by
an internal evaluation

230
00:19:27.083 --> 00:19:29.093
of the heart and lungs,
the digestive organs

231
00:19:29.377 --> 00:19:31.417
and finally, the brain.

232
00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:33.023
We've got some beautiful
weather here

233
00:19:33.047 --> 00:19:34.217
for the next few days.

234
00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:38.427
Subject is
in her mid to late 20s.

235
00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.430
Appears to be.

236
00:19:40.722 --> 00:19:44.522
Subject appears to be
in her mid to late 20s.

237
00:19:44.809 --> 00:19:47.439
Caucasian.
Skin appears normal.

238
00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:51.769
No outwards signs
of bleeding or bruising.

239
00:19:52.066 --> 00:19:55.066
No scarring, no distinctive
external markings.

240
00:19:57.947 --> 00:20:00.237
Hair, brown.

241
00:20:00.992 --> 00:20:01.992
Eyes..

242
00:20:04.454 --> 00:20:05.544
...grey?

243
00:20:09.417 --> 00:20:10.537
Huh.

244
00:20:12.754 --> 00:20:14.054
You don't see
clouding like that

245
00:20:14.339 --> 00:20:15.969
unless a body's been dead
for days.

246
00:20:19.928 --> 00:20:22.348
There's no lividity.

247
00:20:22.639 --> 00:20:24.059
No rigor mortis either.

248
00:20:24.349 --> 00:20:25.809
When do you think she died?

249
00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:28.020
Well, she's colder
than the ambient temperature.

250
00:20:28.311 --> 00:20:29.651
What, conditions
at the scene?

251
00:20:29.938 --> 00:20:31.858
Could be confounding factors.

252
00:20:32.148 --> 00:20:34.148
Look how small her waist is.

253
00:20:34.567 --> 00:20:36.487
Like it doesn't really fit
the rest of her frame.

254
00:20:36.736 --> 00:20:37.736
Could be congenital.

255
00:20:37.904 --> 00:20:39.264
We won't know
until we open her up.

256
00:20:39.447 --> 00:20:41.617
Mark it down on the board.
We'll come back to it later.

257
00:21:09.686 --> 00:21:11.516
Her wrists and ankles
are fractured.

258
00:21:13.064 --> 00:21:15.404
How do you break
your wrists and ankles

259
00:21:15.692 --> 00:21:17.322
without any outward signs?

260
00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:19.530
Oh, I see it all the time.

261
00:21:19.821 --> 00:21:20.821
Simple fractures.

262
00:21:20.989 --> 00:21:23.569
Simple? Uh-uh.
Her joints are shattered.

263
00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:30.160
What is that?
What is it? Dirt?

264
00:21:30.456 --> 00:21:32.706
No, no, this is denser.

265
00:21:33.001 --> 00:21:35.211
